<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian bankruptcies jump 26 percent in 1996/97.</title>
<headline>Australian bankruptcies jump 26 percent in 1996/97.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of Australians declared bankrupt  jumped 26.1 percent in the fiscal year to June 30, rising to 21,846  from 17,324 the year earlier, according to government statistics released  on Friday.</p>
<p>The figures also showed the number of bankruptcies in the June quarter  1997 increased 22.47 percent to 5,936 from 4,847 in the same quarter  a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Canberra Bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
</text>
